
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  blue-data-web-source — Single-URL vs BFS Crawl
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  APPROACH A — Single-URL ingest (WEB.INGEST)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ingested 1 URL: https://blog.example.com/
  Chunks produced: 1

    chunk 00  § Tech Blog
           Welcome to our technology blog covering artificial intelligence, quant…

  Observation: only the index page is processed.
  Linked article pages are NOT followed.

  APPROACH B — BFS crawl (WEB.CRAWL, depth=1, same_domain_only=True)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Seed URL: https://blog.example.com/
  Pages crawled: 4
  Chunks produced: 7

     1 chunks  |  https://blog.example.com/  (Tech Blog)
     2 chunks  |  https://blog.example.com/ai-trends  (AI Trends 2026)
     2 chunks  |  https://blog.example.com/quantum  (Quantum Computing Update)
     2 chunks  |  https://blog.example.com/robotics  (Robotics in 2026)

  External domain 'https://external.example.org/news' was NOT crawled (same_domain_only=True).

  COMPARISON
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Approach                   Pages  Chunks
  ───────────────────────── ────── ───────
  WEB.INGEST (single URL)        1       1
  WEB.CRAWL (depth=1)            4       7

  When to use each:
   • WEB.INGEST  — known URL, single article, or API response page
   • WEB.CRAWL   — documentation sites, blogs, multi-page reports
     depth=1 follows links from seed only; depth=2 follows links of links
     max_pages limits total pages regardless of depth
     same_domain_only=True (default) prevents crawling external sites

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

